ned environments (resource sizing per model-registry-operator reference, benchmark-informed).\n- HLR-6 (P2?): Migration path from default vector store to production-grade vector DB — this is an Open Question in the strategy (\"Should users have a migration path...?\"). Does the answer change which epics exist? Not really — it's a future consideration; the Staff input doesn't address it beyond portability design (BFF should consume shared connection string in 3.6 — that's portability of the app, not user data migration). The migration-path open question: answer doesn't change current epics (validating/deciding it is not gating). Handle as acceptance criterion / note? Per Step 3 decision rule: NO → acceptance criterion on relevant epic. Hmm, or health warning. I'll treat it as a noted open question handled via AC on branch epics (\"design does not preclude future migration; document limitations\") — actually that's inventing scope. Better: note in Health Warnings that the migration-path open question is deferred (does not gate epic structure; Staff input scoped the default store to dev experimentation with external vector DB recommended for production, which addresses the spirit). I'll mention in summary and as a note, not an AC. Actually the Staff input says \"Users with production-scale vector workloads should use an external vector database\" — that resolves the migration question directionally. I'll record it as resolved-by-staff-input in the summary.\n\nAlso the scoping model open question (per-namespace vs per-instance) — Staff: per-namespace preferred for isolation; Auto Rag needed per-instance but Auto Rag is decoupled. So resolved: per-namespace. Note in summary as staff-resolution.\n\nEffort/sizing: not available (attachment missing).\n\nEpic count: main plan = E001 (Investigation), E002 (Implementation, OGX Core). Branch epics: BRANCH-A-E003, BRANCH-B-E003, BRANCH-C-E003. epic_count: \"may count either main-plan epics only or all epics including branches\" 