h the evidence evaluated and the conditional plan for the selected approach\n- If a fallback is selected, document the deviation from the out-of-the-box requirement and the impact on the inline-provider removal work that this strategy unblocks\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A decision record exists that selects exactly one of the three provisioning approaches for RHOAI 3.5\n- The record states the go/no-go criteria evaluated (dashboard operator modularization delivery status, release timing, lifecycle-management risk) and the evidence used for each\n- The go/no-go gate is defined, executed, and its outcome communicated as part of sprint planning\n- If the operator-based path is not selected, the record names the selected fallback and documents the deviation from the out-of-the-box, no-manual-setup requirement\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0 — default vector store available out-of-the-box): this decision determines the mechanism by which the out-of-the-box store is delivered, and whether the requirement is met directly or via a documented fallback\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":72822,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab54d2061dd61d3e","agent_id":"a1996eff85dd3732e","session_id":"02e875f2-6cfe-4933-bc28-36b9ef9ef3bb","uuid":"cf40a3e3-de9a-4b62-a79a-a024fc4ea1f4","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:42:16.774Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004 into epics"}
