{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ed0c7e5b-897b-44e6-b99f-7b10c0eeb0cb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a811142a943d2c2b","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-xqjz7889/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E003.md","content":"# Operator-Based PostgreSQL/pgvector Self-Provisioning for Gen AI Studio Playgrounds\n\n## Description\n\nSelected if the provisioning go/no-go decision chooses the operator-based path — i.e., the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) lands in time for RHOAI 3.5. This epic implements PostgreSQL/pgvector lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer that the modularization delivers, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioning pattern, so that Gen AI Studio playgrounds with RAG get a working default vector store out of the box with no manual setup. It uses the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL 16 image with pgvector (no custom image build, no Konflux onboarding). RHAISTRAT-7164 is a hard precondition: until it delivers the operator layer, there is no RHOAI-controlled operator where PostgreSQL lifecycle management can live — the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic cannot start until the provisioning go/no-go decision selects the operator-based outcome. It consumes the pgvector provider validation, benchmark, and sizing recommendation produced by the OGX distribution work as inputs to its configuration and sizing decisions.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning and lifecycle management (deployment, service, persistent storage, credentials, cleanup on deletion) in the RHOAI-controlled operator, following the model-registry-operator's auto-provisioned-database pattern\n- Wire the vector_io configuration of OGX instances created for playgrounds to the provisioned pgvector store, scoped per namespace for multi-tenant isolation\n- Apply resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's PostgreSQL reference sizing, adjusted per the benchmark results\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC becomes available (RHOAI 3.6), the provisioning must be able to consume a shared connection string instead of self-provisioning\n- Provide a configuration path to point playground RAG at an external, production-grade vector database for users whose workloads outgrow the default store\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Configuring a Gen AI Studio playground with RAG provisions a pgvector-backed PostgreSQL instance automatically, with no manual user setup of external infrastructure\n- Provisioned vector stores are isolated per namespace; one tenant's playground cannot access another namespace's vector data\n- End-to-end Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval, grounded generation) function with the provisioned pgvector store with no loss of current capability compared to the inline provider\n- Deleting a playground cleans up the provisioned PostgreSQL resources (deployment, service, storage, secrets)\n- The provisioned instance's resource requests/limits fit the resource-constrained-environment envelope defined by the benchmark-informed sizing recommendation\n- The design documents how the implementation will consume the shared platform PostgreSQL connection string when it becomes available in RHOAI 3.6, and how a user points playground RAG at an external vector database\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0 — default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning): this epic is the out-of-the-box delivery mechanism for the operator-based outcome\n- HLR-2 (P0 — playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability): end-to-end workflow validation\n- HLR-3 (P0 — vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): the provisioned PostgreSQL runs outside the OGX process\n- HLR-4 (P0 — multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation): namespace-scoped provisioning\n- HLR-5 (P1 — lightweight for resource-constrained environments): reference-based, benchmark-adjusted sizing\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74428,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab54d2061dd61d3e","agent_id":"a1996eff85dd3732e","session_id":"02e875f2-6cfe-4933-bc28-36b9ef9ef3bb","uuid":"a1b923d4-c854-4a6c-a901-71650e554af2","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:42:39.726Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004 into epics"}
