{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-ed0c7e5b-897b-44e6-b99f-7b10c0eeb0cb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9f01e23a43bead91","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-xqjz7889/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-C-E003.md","content":"# Bring-Your-Own PostgreSQL Configuration for Playground RAG\n\n## Description\n\nSelected if the provisioning go/no-go decision chooses the bring-your-own fallback — i.e., the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does not land in time for RHOAI 3.5 and the team requires customers to supply their own PostgreSQL for RAG capabilities in the playground. This is the documented deviation from the out-of-the-box requirement: users manually configure the OGX instance for their playground with their own PostgreSQL/pgvector connection details. This aligns with the breaking changes introduced in OGX 1.0, even though the playground largely abstracts OGX from users. This epic is a contingency: if selected, it should be re-prioritized to P0, because it becomes the only path preserving playground RAG functionality when inline providers are removed.\n\n## Description of Dependencies\n\nThis epic cannot start until the provisioning go/no-go decision selects the bring-your-own outcome. It consumes the pgvector provider validation and configuration knowledge produced by the OGX distribution work.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Provide the configuration surface by which a user supplies external PostgreSQL/pgvector connection details (including the connection-string secret) for the vector_io provider of the OGX instance backing their playground\n- Validate that Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows function against a user-provided pgvector instance\n- Document the setup steps and the deviation from the out-of-the-box experience, including the recommendation that production-scale vector workloads use an external vector database\n- Confirm the configuration path also serves users who deliberately choose an external, production-grade vector database instead of the default store\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- A user can configure external PostgreSQL/pgvector connection details for their playground's OGX instance via a supported configuration surface, with credentials supplied through a secret\n- Gen AI Studio playground RAG workflows (document upload, embedding, retrieval, grounded generation) function against the user-provided pgvector instance with no loss of current capability compared to the inline provider\n- Setup documentation exists for the bring-your-own path, states the manual steps required, and records the deviation from the no-manual-setup requirement\n- The configured vector store runs as a separate process from the OGX instance (no inline vector provider in the serving path)\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P0 — default vector store available out-of-the-box): documented deviation — this outcome requires manual setup by design; the deviation is recorded in the decision and in this epic's documentation deliverable\n- HLR-2 (P0 — playground RAG workflows function with no loss of current capability): preserved via user-provided infrastructure\n- HLR-3 (P0 — vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance): external PostgreSQL by construction\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74428,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ab54d2061dd61d3e","agent_id":"a1996eff85dd3732e","session_id":"02e875f2-6cfe-4933-bc28-36b9ef9ef3bb","uuid":"684a6a4c-a4b5-43bd-bbd2-609b8c38f816","timestamp":"2026-10-26T20:42:57.790Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004 into epics"}
